WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:08.382
Hi!

00:00:08.438 --> 00:00:09.210
I'm Ana.

00:00:09.289 --> 00:00:10.822
Welcome to 'What to Say'!

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:34.483
Do you know what to say when you want to ask a favour?

00:00:34.523 --> 00:00:38.078
Listen out for useful language for asking a favour.

00:00:38.578 --> 00:00:41.711
 Then, we'll practise saying the new phrases –

00:00:41.797 --> 00:00:43.218
after this.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.601
Paul, have you got a minute?

00:00:47.656 --> 00:00:48.806
I need a favour.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:51.408
I'm a bit busy, but sure,

00:00:51.837 --> 00:00:53.033
what can I help you with?

00:00:53.479 --> 00:00:57.244
So, you know the branding job for Active Arctic?

00:00:57.518 --> 00:01:00.737
Of course. It was so good to finally finish that project.

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.688
It went on and on and on ...

00:01:02.751 --> 00:01:04.149
Yeah, so …

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.087
Look, I'm really sorry about this,

00:01:07.204 --> 00:01:09.813
but they want some more changes made.

00:01:10.025 --> 00:01:11.025
Seriously?

00:01:11.636 --> 00:01:16.205
I've already rewritten that copy, I don't know, like, 20 times?

00:01:16.237 --> 00:01:18.768
I know. I'm so sorry.

00:01:19.284 --> 00:01:22.127
Would you be able to work on it this afternoon?

00:01:22.175 --> 00:01:24.449
Well, I'm not really sure if I can, Noelia.

00:01:24.512 --> 00:01:29.863
I'm finishing the Moosh Monkey social media campaign and they're expecting it by the end of the day.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.887
I'd forgotten about that.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:38.933
Is there any chance you could work late tonight?

00:01:38.949 --> 00:01:42.832
Sorry, Noelia. I would if I could, but I can't.

00:01:45.254 --> 00:01:45.972
Please?

00:01:45.996 --> 00:01:50.692
I'm taking my niece to the cinema for her birthday. It's been planned for ages.

00:01:50.716 --> 00:01:56.371
OK. Well, then could you come in early tomorrow?

00:01:56.786 --> 00:01:58.215
I'll make it up to you!

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.700
OK.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:00.850
How?

00:02:02.007 --> 00:02:03.256
Name your price.

00:02:04.061 --> 00:02:05.595
An extra day's holiday?

00:02:06.053 --> 00:02:07.787
Can you get in for 5 a.m.?

00:02:07.938 --> 00:02:08.906
7 a.m.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.522
6 a.m.

00:02:11.508 --> 00:02:12.424
Deal.

00:02:14.005 --> 00:02:15.005
Deal.

00:02:18.266 --> 00:02:19.266
Hello again!

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.990
 Looks like that's an early start for Paul tomorrow, then!

00:02:23.225 --> 00:02:28.061
So, did you notice the useful phrases used for asking a favour?

00:02:28.546 --> 00:02:30.748
Listen to me and then repeat.

00:02:31.476 --> 00:02:32.943
Have you got a minute?

00:02:35.172 --> 00:02:36.562
Have you got a minute?

00:02:38.586 --> 00:02:39.786
